ith fibrous tissue  The remainder of the  breast tissue is comprised of unremarkable adipose tissue with focal hemorrhage  from the area of the needle with thin bands of fibrous tissue running  throughout  The breast is composed of approximately 95  adipose tissue  The  nodule identified on the radiograph is entirely submitted  The second fibrous  area is also entirely submitted  Representative sections from the distant  margins are submitted for histologic evaluation  Approximately 50  of the  breast tissue has been submitted for histologic evaluation   Micro REMOVED_DATE  radiographically identified lesion  multi frags  ESS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  second firm nodule in medial aspect  multi frags  ESS   Micro 11  inferior margin  2 frags  RSS   Micro 12  lateral margin  2 frags  RSS   Micro 13  anterior margin  2 frags  RSS   rp  Reports to  SHOJI  BRENT  T  M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS   report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 39 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  1 CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 40                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of breast which is inked and sectioned to reveal a vague 1 0cm stellate firm gritty area extending to the inked margin  Representative sections of the tumor are submitted in cassette A through C  Representative sections of the remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassette D through F  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  FIRM AREA  HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
