Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Hem Malignancies  YAW 7    Path Subspecialty Service  Hemepath  Results To  SADHNA VORA  M D   ALEXANDRA E KOVACH  M D   Resident  Alexandra Kovach  M D   Signed Out by  Robert Hasserjian  M D              Addended Report                Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Special Stains   CLINICAL DATA   Possible myeloma       FINAL DIAGNOSIS   BONE MARROW  LEFT ILIAC   BIOPSY  ASPIRATE AND PERIPHERAL SMEAR   HYPOCELLULAR MARROW WITH MINIMAL INVOLVEMENT BY A PLASMA CELL NEOPLASM  SEE  NOTE AND SUMMARY      NOTE  The bone marrow biopsy specimen is fragmented and hemorrhagic  The  marrow cellularity is overall 15 20   The myeloid to erythroid ratio is  decreased  Myeloid maturation is complete  Erythroid maturation is complete   Megakaryocytes are adequate  Interstitial atypical plasma cells are  identified  scattered and in small clusters  with round nuclei  coarse  chromatin  and abundant cytoplasm with perinuclear clearing  Occasional  binucleate plasma cells are noted and many forms have intranuclear inclusions   Dutcher bodies   Immunohistochemical stains demonstrate that approximately 5   of the marrow cellularity is composed of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   plasma cells  scattered and in  small interstitial clusters  In situ hybridization for kappa and lambda  immunoglobulin light chains demonstrates an excess of lambda positive plasma  cells compared to kappa positive cells  mainly seen in the clustered plasma  cells  the scattered single plasma cells appear to be polytypic  Selected  markers were evaluated by immunohistochemistry as well as flow cytometry to  assess their expression in the context of the tissue architecture  Both H E and Giemsa stains were examined to evaluate this specimen     The aspirate smear is adequate for evaluation  A 400 cell count reveals  32   myeloid precursors  46  erythroid precursors  10  lymphocytes  1  monocytes  4   eosinophils  0  basophils  1  promyelocytes  1  blasts  and 5  plasma cells   Myeloid maturation is normal  Erythroid maturation is generally normal with  rare late mitoses and nuclear irregularities  Megakaryocytes are normal   Plasma cells are medium to large with round nuclei  coarse chromatin   occasional prominent nucleoli and abundant basophilic cytoplasm  Many  erythroid elements appear    degenerate  apparently representing a     staining processing artifact     CBC results from REMOVED_DATE are as follows  WBC 3 7  HCT 37 0   PLT 253  Auto  differential  54  polys  37  lymphs  5  monos  4  eos  0  basos  Review of the  peripheral smear reveals occasional reactive lymphocytes  no circulating plasma  cells are identified     SUMMARY  The overall findings demonstrate a small burden of marrow involvement  by a monotypic lambda plasma cell neoplasm  However  in the absence of  myeloma related symptoms  the degree of involvement is insufficient for a  diagnosis of plasma cell myeloma  No amyloid is seen on routine histology   results of a Congo red stain will be reported in an addendum       GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received in B  fixative   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm brown firm tissue core submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   after decalcification Also  received is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of blood coagulum submitted in toto  as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID        Final Diagnosis by Robert Hasserjian M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday  REMOVED_MONTH 22   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 08 28PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses       ADDENDUM NOTE   A reticulin stain shows 1  4 fiber staining  A Congo Red stain fails to reveal  amyloid material  The diagnosis is unchanged           Addendum  1 by Robert Hasserjian M D   Electronically signed on Thursday  REMOVED_MONTH 01   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 58 19PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses     PART A  Bone Marrow  Left   Biopsy  PART B  Bone Marrow  Aspirate   Smear  PART C  Peripheral Blood  Smear       report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
