of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab in two separately labeled parts  Labeled  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire in place  inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Submitted entirely in A through I  Labeled  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Submitted entirely in J through R  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST PART B  RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
