Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 01 CLINICAL DATA  51 year old female who presents with an inflamed breast with dimpling  Rule out inflammatory carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSIES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  75    MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  25    COMEDO AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  BOTH SPECIMENS  WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE  2  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 4cm in greatest dimension on histologic section  slide C  in the larger breast biopsy and 1 3cm in greatest dimension  slide A  in the smaller breast biopsy  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 20 36                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 MAY 95 at 15 13     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  LEFT   Ten percent of the tumor cells stain for c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   favorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  unlabeled  specimen confirmed with Dr  Ferguson via personal communication  consisting of two pieces of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  respectively  the former with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm diffusely tan white skin ellipse with a central red punctate depression  The specimens are inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous  slightly gritty breast tissue  A representative section from the larger portion is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  A representative section of the smaller portion is frozen as frozen section  2  and resubmitted in A  The remaining larger portion of breast tissue is submitted entirely in B through F  with the ends of the skin ellipse in B through C  and the smaller portion of breast tissue in G through I  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  LEFT BREAST  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene 