Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 36 CLINICAL DATA  71 year old female with three areas of suspicious calcifications on left mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SINGLE FOCUS ON ONE OF TEN SLIDES  H   ABUTTING A POSTERIOR  GREEN  MARGIN  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH MODERATE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   1   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 19 OF 19 NODES  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   2   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 39                                                                                     ADDITIONAL TISSUE Addendum     NOTE  At the request of Dr  Barbara Smith  this case is reviewed for the presence of microcalcifications or additional atypical foci  The initial slides are reviewed and additional tissue sections submitted in R Z and AA BB  Scattered and occasionally dense calcifications are identified in 8 of the 11 additional slides  localized to areas of fibrocystic change and hyperplasia  No additional foci of ductal carcinoma in situ are identified  other than the single focus on section H  Added by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 7 x 7 x 2cm piece of fatty tissue with three localization wires and a short stitch designating the superior aspect  and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  The specimen is inked black  with the anterior surface over inked blue and the posterior surface over inked green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal the absence of gross lesions suspicious for invasive carcinoma  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through J  from lateral to medial aspects  with A the most lateral  J the most medial  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a 8 x 6 x 2cm aggregate of unremarkable adipose tissue  A lymph node dissection is performed with lymph nodes submitted in K through P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of adipose tissue with one lymph node  The lymph node is bisected and the specimen is entirely submitted in cassette Q  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST EXCISION   NO INVASIVE CARCINOMA GROSSLY IDENTIFIED  O R  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  2   EXCISION   report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
