ult was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab and accompanied with specimen radiograph   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm segment of fibrofatty breast tissue with a localizing wire  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm  tan white  firm  stellate mass which is 0 3cm from the inked margin  Representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  The remainder was entirely submitted in cassettes A through K with suspicious area in A through F  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  EXTENSIVE INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES AND A SUSPICIOUS FOCUS OF INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
